-- title:
--   O[[X]]/(X-varpi) is a complete discrete valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain and a discrete valuation ring, and let $\varpi \in O$ be an irreducible element. Consider the quotient $W := O[[X]]/(X - C(\varpi))$ of the formal power series ring in one variable over $O$ by the principal ideal generated by $X - \varpi$, where $\varpi$ is viewed as a constant power series. The theorem asserts, as a single existential statement whose witnesses are instances on $W$ together with a final property, that: $W$ is an integral domain; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; $W$ is complete for the adic filtration by the powers of its maximal ideal, in the sense of `IsAdicComplete` (Hausdorff and precomplete for that ideal); and the image of the constant power series $C(\varpi)$ under the quotient map $O[[X]] \to W$ is an irreducible element of $W$, i.e. a uniformiser. The hypothesis that $\varpi$ is irreducible is used throughout; in particular it is what makes the class of $C(\varpi)$ a nonzero nonunit.
--
--   This identifies $O[[X]]/(X-\varpi)$ as a complete discrete valuation ring with uniformiser the class of $\varpi$ — concretely, the $\varpi$-adic completion of $O$ presented by a power series variable specialising to $\varpi$. It supplies the coefficient ring of the crossing models $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \bar\varpi^{\,E})$ used for completed local rings at the nodes of modular curves, and is cited by the statements producing ring isomorphisms of adic completions with such models and by the prolongation-tuple constructions over them.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PowerSeries_isAdicComplete_quotient_span_X_sub_C_of_irreducible.lean

